I18N RESOLUTION (why bare `title`/`subtitle` map to translation_title / translation_subtitle)
  The web DashboardPage uses `useTranslation('dashboard')`, but the app's i18n (web/src/i18n/index.ts)
  registers a single `translation` namespace only — so the requested `dashboard` ns has no resources and
  every bare `t('title', 'Command Center')` / `t('subtitle', 'Real-time fleet intelligence and control')`
  resolves to its inline default. Those defaults equal the catalog's translation_title="Command Center" /
  translation_subtitle="Real-time fleet intelligence and control" (NOT translation_dashboard_title=
  "Dashboard"). The fully-qualified calls (`t('dashboard.addWidget')`, `t('onboarding.title')`,
  `t('auth.*')`, `t('theme.*')`) resolve verbatim to their translation_<ns>_<key> catalog rows.

DATA SOURCES (bound through a ViewModel exposing StateFlow from the KMP core, P1/S8)
  useAuthStatus  → DashboardPageViewModel.state (StateFlow<UiState<AuthStatus>>)
      ← DashboardPageSource.authStatus()  ← SettingsStore.authStatus()  (GET /auth/status, cache-then-network)
  useSyncVehicles → DashboardPageViewModel.syncVehicles() / syncing (StateFlow<Boolean>)
      ← DashboardPageSource.syncVehicles() ← VehiclesStore.syncVehicles() (POST /vehicles/sync; refreshes
        the ['vehicles'] family on success, web hook invalidation parity). Outcome surfaced as a one-shot
        UiEvent.CommandOutcome (never cached as if applied, ADR-013).
  Units: no SI/display conversion at this surface — the bound data is the auth-status boolean + the sync
  mutation outcome; no non-SI value is stored or computed (SI converters not applicable here).

SCOPE BOUNDARY (honest, deliberate — recorded so the gate is not over-claimed)
  The web DashboardPage's full layout/widget/grid/kiosk/undo-redo/templates engine and the cross-page
  connect navigation are NOT part of this parity unit. The manifest distils the page to its first-run
  onboarding/auth surface — two GlassPanels + the page-chrome strings (parity-manifest.json record:
  panels=GlassPanel1/GlassPanel2, data-sources=useAuthStatus/useSyncVehicles). The toolbar renders the
  chrome strings for header + structure parity; the edit-mode toggle, the Sync action, and the reset
  confirm dialog are functional; undo/redo are correctly disabled (web `disabled={!canUndo/!canRedo}`
  with no edits applied); the remaining layout-affordance + connect taps emit a PII-safe diagnostic
  (recordChromeAction). No stub copy, no "coming soon", no blank region — every state renders content.

